<title>UK: EMI chief exec Fifield exercises options.</title>
<headline>EMI chief exec Fifield exercises options.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>EMI Group Plc said chief executive James Fifield on Monday exercised options for 126,542 shares and immediately sold all the shares acquired, making an almost 100 percent profit.</p>
<p>Fifield exercised the options for the 126,542 shares at a price of 740.47 pence a share, for a total price of 937,006 stg. He sold the shares at a price of 1450 pence each for a total of 1,834,859 stg, the company said.</p>
<p>The options exercised were adjusted to reflect the demerger last month of the EMI music business from the Thorn rentals business.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
